{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978760-a-fork-in-the-road-path-hack-brainstorming","id":978760,"title":"A Fork in the Road (Path Hack Brainstorming)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T18:29:30-07:00","id":978760,"title":"A Fork in the Road (Path Hack Brainstorming)","content":"Idle thinking got me curious, so I'm bringing this forumside as a thought experiment. This is effectively a narrower version of the Warlocks of Arcadia systems hack from the Chronicler's Guide, but the fact that it's effectively only doubling the number of distinct Paths is part of why I wanted to try and hash this out.<br /> <br /> In essence, the change is simple: Like WoA, each Path has a consistent Subtle Arcanum \u2014 the Obrimos all have Prime, the Acanthus all have Fate, et cetera \u2014 but the Gross Arcanum is changed to a pick from the orthodox route (like, say, Space for the Mastigos) or that of the next Path along the Supernal Pentacle model (e.g. Matter for the Thyrsus or Forces for the Moros).<br /> <br /> So the basic change results in the following Ruling Arcana for the Paths:<br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus:</b> <i>Fate</i>, Time/Space<br /> <b>Mastigos:</b> <i>Mind</i>, Space/Life<br /> <b>Moros:</b> <i>Death</i>, Matter/Forces<br /> <b>Obrimos:</b> <i>Prime</i>, Forces/Time<br /> <b>Thyrsus:</b> <i>Spirit</i>, Life/Matter<br /> <br /> What knock-on effects does this alteration suggest? Do the Manifest Beings of a given Path's Supernal Realm need a division or subdivision of nomenclature to account for the split? Should the extra dot in a Resistance Attribute be allocated in some way based on the choice of second Ruling Arcanum? Are the abilities afforded by easier learning of a separate Arcanum across half of a Path likely to affect the symbolism and stereotypes of that class of mage? (Feel free to add your own questions here.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:45:24-07:00","id":979360,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Manifest Beings need to change; IMO those are based on the Arcanum itself, rather than the Path.<br /> <br /> And... while it certainly affects the symbolism and stereotype of each Path, I think that they work fine with that additional option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}